<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benjamin Franklin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1706–1790</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benjamin Franklin was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> printer, writer, scientist and statesman. He founded a library, a fire company and the academy that became the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, and became famous for his experiments with electricity. He helped draft the Declaration of Independence, won the French alliance and negotiated the peace of 1783. A breakaway state beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appalachian-mountains">Appalachians</a> was named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin.jpg" alt="Benjamin Franklin" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph-Siffred Duplessis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Siffrein_Duplessis_-_Benjamin_Franklin_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
